# EtButtonGroup Component

## Purpose & Scope

`EtButtonGroup` is a horizontal group of icon buttons for the eToro design system. It provides:

- **Compound component pattern**: `EtButtonGroup.Item` subcomponent for each button
- **Pill-shaped container**: Rounded ends on first/last items
- **Smooth press animations**: Animated background color transitions using Reanimated
- **Haptic feedback**: Enabled by default on press

**Does NOT handle:**

- Toggle/selection states (buttons are action-only)
- Text labels (icon-only buttons)
- Variable sizing (fixed height of 36px)

## Entry Points & Contracts

### `EtButtonGroup` (main component)

```tsx
<EtButtonGroup style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle> testID?: string>
  {children}
</EtButtonGroup>
```

**Children constraints:** Only `<EtButtonGroup.Item>` components are valid (enforced at runtime).

### `EtButtonGroup.Item`

```tsx
<EtButtonGroup.Item
  iconName: IconName           // required
  onPress: () => void          // required
  disabled?: boolean           // default: false
  testID?: string
  accessibilityLabel?: string
/>
```

## Usage

```tsx
<EtButtonGroup>
  <EtButtonGroup.Item iconName="priceAlert" onPress={handlePriceAlert} />
  <EtButtonGroup.Item iconName="expand" onPress={handleExpand} />
</EtButtonGroup>
```

## Anti-patterns

❌ **Non-Item children** - Only `EtButtonGroup.Item` allowed, other elements throw runtime error

❌ **Item outside EtButtonGroup** - Missing context will throw error

❌ **Text labels** - Use `EtButton` or `EtChip` for buttons with text

## Design System Integration

- **Colors** (from `useEtoroTheme().colors`):
  - Normal: `bgButtonGroupNormal` (Light: Neutral/50 `#F2F2F2`, Dark: Neutral/800 `#333333`)
  - Pressed: `bgButtonGroupPressed` (Light: Neutral/600@25% `#66666625`, Dark: Neutral/600@25% `#66666625`)
  - Icon: `textPrimaryNeutral`
  - Disabled: 50% opacity
- **Spacing** (from `etoro-ui/core/styles`):
  - Padding: `X3` (12px)
  - Border radius: `X8` (32px)
  - Icon size: `X5` (20px)
  - Height: `X9` (36px)
  - Gap: 2px

## Patterns & Pitfalls

### Context Architecture

- `ButtonGroupProvider` wraps each item with `isFirst` and `isLast` flags
- Position determines border radius (rounded on first/last only)

### Animation

- 150ms transition using `interpolateColor` with `withTiming`
- Always cleanup animations on unmount with `cancelAnimation`

### Haptic Feedback

- `ImpactFeedbackStyle.Light` on press (disabled buttons excluded)

## Development Learnings

### Use Design System Tokens

Never hardcode values. Use spacing constants (`X3`, `X5`, `X8`, `X9`) and theme colors (`colors.bgGreyTransparentPrimary`).

### Animation Cleanup

Always cleanup Reanimated animations on unmount:

```typescript
useEffect(() => {
  return () => {
    cancelAnimation(pressed);
  };
}, [pressed]);
```

### Theme Reactivity

Use `useDerivedValue` for colors to ensure theme changes (dark/light mode) are reflected:

```typescript
const colors = useDerivedValue(() => [normalColor, pressedColor]);

const animatedStyle = useAnimatedStyle(() => ({
  backgroundColor: interpolateColor(pressed.value, [0, 1], colors.value),
}));
```

### Component-Specific Animation Timing

Different components need different animation durations (ButtonGroup: 150ms, Checkbox: 300ms). Keep animation constants per-component in `utils/animation-constants.ts`.

### Testing

Tests require mocks for:

- `useEtoroTheme` - provide mock colors
- `EtoroIcon` - mock component
- `expo-haptics` - mock haptic feedback
- `cancelAnimation` - patch the existing Reanimated mock:

```typescript
const reanimatedModule = jest.requireMock('react-native-reanimated');
if (reanimatedModule && !reanimatedModule.cancelAnimation) {
  reanimatedModule.cancelAnimation = jest.fn();
}
```
